  "goodToKnow": "Besagen is a formal verb for things that say or indicate something, such as a law or a document: Die Regel besagt, dass... It isn't used for people talking. The participle besagt also works as an adjective in formal language: die besagte Person (the person in question). Das besagt nichts means that doesn't mean anything. For people, use sagen or erklären. It's inseparable, so no ge- in the participle."
